# The root .gitignore has a bare `model/` rule for the top-level dev directory.
# A bare rule matches at every depth, so it also swallowed `go/pkg/model/` — the
# package holding the download/cache manager was never committed, and a fresh
# clone could not build the Go SDK at all. Re-include it here.
!pkg/model/
!pkg/model/**

# Build output. `go/lib/` held two committed symlinks into a `/home/janakh/...`
# node_modules path that existed on exactly one machine; both were dangling
# everywhere else and nothing in the Go code read them, so they are gone. Do not
# vendor the runtime here — see the ONNX Runtime section of README.md for how the
# shared library is located.
lib/
*.so
*.dylib

# The `go/monocr` binary is still tracked; untracking it is a separate change.
